Usage: main COMMAND [ARGS...]
       main                 # read commands from stdin
       main --help
       main -r DIR [--mtime] [--local|--utc] [--histogram]

Commands:
  cat      Concatenate files to standard output.
  head     Show the first lines of a file or stream.
  tail     Display the last N lines (default 10); never create input files.
  pwd      Print physical working directory.
  stat     Inspect file metadata.
  ls       List directory contents.
  mkdir    Create directories.
  touch    Create empty files or update timestamps without changing contents.
  clear    Clear an ANSI-compatible terminal screen.
  cp       Copy files and directories.
  cd       Change working directory.
  help [COMMAND]  List commands or show command usage.
  exit            Leave the loop with the last command status.
